[[This is a short sample screenplay, not a finished script. The "Key: value" lines at the top make the title page. Notes in double brackets, like this one, stay in the source but never print. Delete them when you're done exploring.]]

# Act One

= Margaret waits up for a call that never comes.

[[A line starting with # is a section, and one starting with = is a synopsis. They build the outline and never print.]]

INT. KITCHEN - NIGHT

[[A scene heading starts with INT. or EXT. and usually ends with the time of day.]]

A small kitchen, cleaner than it needs to be. The wall clock reads 11:40.

MARGARET (60s), cardigan buttoned wrong, sits at the table in front of a plate she hasn't touched. She watches the phone on the wall.

!SILENCE.
Just the clock.

[[Without the ! at the start, SILENCE would read as a character saying "Just the clock." The ! forces the lines to be action.]]

MARGARET
(quietly)
You said you'd call.

[[A name in capitals on its own line, followed directly by speech, is a character cue. A line in parentheses right under the name is a parenthetical.]]

She scrapes the plate into the trash and sets it in the sink harder than she needs to.

A KNOCK at the back door.

DANNY (O.S.)
Mom? It's me. I lost my phone.

[[(O.S.) means off screen: we hear Danny before we see him.]]

Margaret doesn't move.

MARGARET
Of course you did.

She opens the door. DANNY (30s), soaked through, holds out a bakery box gone soft in the rain.

DANNY
I *did* call. From a pay phone. Do you know how hard it is to find a pay phone?

MARGARET
Harder than finding your mother's house, apparently.

He sets the box on the table and lifts the lid. Something that used to be a cake.

[[Margaret speaks again right after a line of action, so Drafter adds (CONT'D) to her name by itself. Don't type it.]]

MARGARET
Is that a cake?

DANNY
It was a cake.

They both start talking at once.

[[A ^ after the second name sets two speeches side by side.]]

MARGARET
You can't just turn up at midnight with--

DANNY ^
I know, I know. I'm sorry. I--

/* MARGARET
You look just like your father when you do that. */

[[Text between /* and */ is cut but kept, in case you want it back. It never prints.]]

They both stop. Margaret hands him a dish towel and, after a long moment, a fork.

CUT TO:

EXT. BACK PORCH - LATER

The rain has stopped. Margaret and Danny sit on the step, eating the ruined cake straight from the box.

DANNY
_Next_ year I'll call from the bakery.

MARGARET
**Next** year you'll come at seven.

[[Single *stars* make italics, double **stars** make bold, and _underscores_ underline. A line wrapped in > and < is centered.]]

> END OF SAMPLE <
